@trait {
  name: "@scheduler",
  category: "system",
  description: "Cron-expression scheduler for time-driven entity behaviors. cron is a standard 5-field or 6-field cron string (e.g. '*/5 * * * *' for every 5 minutes) that governs the tick cadence; the parser supports @hourly/@daily/@weekly/@monthly shortcuts. timezone is the IANA timezone string (e.g. 'America/New_York') used to evaluate the cron expression; defaults to UTC so behavior is deterministic across deployments. enabled is a live gate — setting it false suspends future ticks without detaching the trait; the next tick resumes from the next scheduled time when re-enabled. max_missed caps how many missed fires (e.g. from downtime) are replayed on recovery; 0 replays none, -1 replays all. jitter_ms adds a uniform random jitter in [0, jitter_ms] milliseconds before each fire to spread coordinated entity bursts across the event loop. on_tick fires on each scheduled execution, carrying scheduled_at (ISO-8601 timestamp) and missed_count (fires replayed this cycle). on_error fires when the cron expression is invalid, the timezone is unresolvable, or the host runtime rejects the schedule, carrying reason and raw_expression. Pairs with @timeout_guard to bound runaway tick handlers and @telemetry to track tick latency. Research: SchedulerTrait.ts v5.1, CronTrait.ts.",
  props: {
    cron: string = "* * * * *",
    timezone: string = "UTC",
    enabled: boolean = true,
    max_missed: number = 0,
    jitter_ms: number = 0
  },
  events: {
    attached: "scheduler:attached",
    detached: "scheduler:detached",
    on_tick: "scheduler:tick",
    on_error: "scheduler:error",
    tick_skipped: "scheduler:tick_skipped",
    on_enable: "scheduler:cmd_enable",
    on_disable: "scheduler:cmd_disable"
  },
  behaviors: ["@timeout_guard"]
}
